  "status": "ok",
  "summary_en": "The Feather node reduces abrupt contrast changes by capping how quickly values can change from one pixel to the next. This gives height fields a beveled appearance, and it can extend masks outward or inward without blurring them the way the Blur COP does.",
  "inputs": [
    "source: original layer to feather",
    "mask: optional per-pixel mask amount scaled by the Mask parameter"
  ],
  "key_parameters": [
    "Signature: layer type accepted by the source",
    "Mask: how much of the new value is mixed with the original; default 1 uses only the new value",
    "Feather from High to Low: when on, bright pixels stay and darker neighbors are raised; when off, dark pixels stay and bright pixels are lowered",
    "Include Border: samples initial pixel values from outside the image bounds, which can create an edge mask from constant borders",
    "Feather Direction: Diamond, Square, Octagon, Custom (uses Sweep Directions), or Circle",
    "Sweep Directions: Custom only; selects which of the eight directions apply, allowing one-sided ramp-like feathers",
    "Feather Method: Distance for Unit Change (distance over which a value of 1 changes to 0) or Change per Distance; the two are inverses"
  ],
  "caveats": [
    "To create a tiling texture, turn on Include Border, and the feather may need to be repeated twice"
  ],
  "resume_fr": "Le nœud Feather limite la vitesse de variation d'une valeur d'un pixel à l'autre, ce qui biseaute un champ de hauteur sans le flouter."
}
